From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:28:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: synchronize bandwidth in AP/STA support

When an AP follows a co-located station (repeater), the station's
channel alone is not enough: the AP must also adopt its bandwidth.

wpa_supplicant reports ch_width, center_freq1 and bw320_offset from
the driver on channel switch events and in phy status. hostapd
passes them through apsta_state to freq_info, and uc_wpa_freq_info()
computes segment 0 and the center frequency for all widths,
including 20/40 MHz (USE_HT) and the second 320 MHz block.

A supplied ch_width takes precedence over scanning the generated
config for *_oper_chwidth. The fast path is guarded against a
missing value: ucode evaluates null >= 0 as true, and treating an
absent width as valid made every channel-only reload CSA drop to
20 MHz. uc_wpa_freq_info() rejects a missing width argument instead
of degrading to 20 MHz, bw320_offset falls back to 1 when absent or
invalid, and the CSA freq params are assigned on errno alone so
explicit zero values apply.

Based-on-work-by: Michael-CY Lee <michael-cy.lee@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
